two-consecutive-stagnant-band rule did not trigger.

## 6. Stop condition, surviving coordinates, and next systems

The band computation was stopped at 2026-09-03 21:57 UTC, 134 minutes 58
seconds after the receipt start, reserving the remaining part of the 150-minute
lane for final validation, custody generation, and sealing.  A cumulative
stage-8 trial was interrupted at that point after 47 min 57.77 s of
host-contended execution; its stdout JSON was still zero bytes.  An earlier
lower-priority stage-9 trial was likewise interrupted with zero-byte JSON so
that the contiguous critical path could finish.  Neither interrupted output
is copied into `box/g9966band-20260903`, cited as evidence, or included in the
validated ledger.  The exact accepted stop is therefore stage 7, not stage 8
or 9.

The `delta=2` branch has no next system because its stage-4 ideal is the unit
ideal.  The consistent `delta=5/2` finite quotient has exactly **869** free
coordinates because its residue is zero.  The complete sorted list (869 lines)
is `runs/delta52/stage7-free-coefficients.txt`, SHA-256
`30d4f3e027d4bb1db62dce3b7226e15f0ac8a74654724d0ede595cc0d10bbbe9`.

The exact next system is supplied as
`runs/delta52/next-stage8-system.json`, SHA-256
`a050af8c5d4bbb703babb2ce2ee57a70c411eb801226ac9f5cdcffbfa0bfa699`.
It contains the same 869 generator names, the accepted stage-7 JSON hash, the
frozen-input dependency, the pinned engine hash, and executable argv.  Its
next band is pole local power 16 with `(F,G)=(-173,-110)`, no further retained
outer `D1` offset, and all 156 coefficients `k=0,...,155` of Jacobian degree
155.  The exact executable definition is

```text
python3 box/g9966band-20260903/band_engine.py --branch delta52 --stage 8
```

with engine SHA-256
`3bd2937d75d59d59edeca1b89eba286fd2711f2d608109e7fd8971b64e059ac9`.
The manifest is deliberately an executable definition, not a claim that it
serializes expanded equations or the unavailable full inverse from `K2c` to
the original `C2,C3` coordinates.

The surviving names are coordinates in the declared `K2c`/outer basis.  They
are called free only when the residual ideal is zero.  If a nonzero polynomial
residue
appears, the report instead lists unresolved quotient generators and the
localized Krull dimension, avoiding the false claim that a nonlinear scheme
is an affine coordinate space.

## 7. Singular and consistency controls

For a nonzero polynomial residue the generated Singular ring is over
characteristic zero
with `dp` ordering on the active generators followed by the wrapper.  The
ideal includes `Zrho*rho-1` or `Zc*c-1`.  The wrapper controls are

```text
<p,Zp-1>       -> unit ideal,
<p-1,Zp-1>     -> nonunit ideal.
```

The raw residue's unit status is recorded rather than assumed.  A branch is
declared `DEAD` only if the localized exact ideal is the unit ideal.  Otherwise
the Singular codimension is subtracted from the post-`Q*` generator count.
For the `delta=2` death, an independent replay of the generated Singular file
prints `dim=-1`, basis `1`, and controls `0,1,0`: the deliberately empty
control and the raw constant ideal are unit, while the point control is
nonunit.  No modular rank is promoted to an exact result.

