+
+All 66 cumulative pivot coefficients parse as nonzero rationals, and none uses c. There are no retired pivot pairs. Before inspecting the residue, the formal remaining-generator count is
+
+    102 inner + 826 outer - 66 joint-Q* = 862.
+
+That number is **not** the dimension of a family. The cumulative 1,285 row labels account as 66 pivots, 1,218 zero/dependent rows, and one nonzero residue; 66+1218+1=1285. There were 1,040 initially nonzero row expressions. The complete labeled-row hash is 56dbca47ef766b098f5d65321324f85909a4c9a65d1a1c10079240b41f5c9ec6, and the one-row reduced-residue hash is e356693da067de90565ae0275ecd5d6779737e962b9d01476fc46b355ce3ccb4.
+
+Because the residue is a unit, the JSON correctly records exact_Krull_dimension_localized=null, verdict=DEAD, and free_coordinate_list_is_valid=false. The legacy boolean nonlinear_residue_appears means only “residue nonempty”; here its residue is a constant, not a nonlinear equation. The 862 unresolved names are therefore not surviving coordinates and are not reported as an affine family.
+
+GNU time records 1,675.06 user seconds, 0.60 system seconds, 95% CPU, 29:17.86 elapsed, 279,160 KiB maximum RSS, and exit status 0. The JSON's earlier internal snapshot was 1,743.065 seconds and 226,040 KiB. As in the charged protocol, the external cumulative-invocation wall and RSS figures in the table are authoritative. stage8.err is empty.
+
+## 4. Constant-unit certificate and Singular replay
+
+After all Q-star substitutions, the exact normal form of the named stage-8 pole row is the integer 64. There is no vanished leader or parameter division hidden in this step: the pivot ledger uses only the rational coefficients in the preceding table and excludes the localization parameter. Over Q, 64 is invertible, proving directly that the raw residue ideal and every localization of it are the unit ideal.
+
+The engine nevertheless emitted the required characteristic-zero Rabinowitsch check:
+
+    ring R=0,(c,Zc),dp;
+    ideal I=64,Zc*c-1;
+    ideal S=std(I);
+
+The independently rerun file returned
+
+    BEGIN_DIM
+    -1
+    END_DIM
+    BEGIN_GB
+    1
+    END_GB
+    BEGIN_CONTROLS
+    0
+    1
+    0
+    END_CONTROLS
+
+Here reduce(1,std(<c,Zc*c-1>))=0 is the deliberately empty control, reduce(1,std(<c-1,Zc*c-1>))=1 is the nonempty point control, and reduce(1,std(<64>))=0 confirms that the raw residue is already unit. Thus the wrapper was applied in the declared ring and both positive and negative controls behaved correctly. The emitted Singular file has SHA-256 36f7f21f9faa3f7fec6b1d9353a194c17c6aecb8d2a5c2e48096b680c6e77b2e; the independent output has SHA-256 236517b4a8e5567c586d39194059d49207001416a1d922efaec1fc3d2b9c7b73.
+
+The modular-then-exact nonlinear-residue path was not activated. The sole residue was classified exactly as a nonzero rational constant before any nonlinear solving question arose, and the authoritative characteristic-zero Singular computation was run twice: inside the engine and independently.
+
+box/g9966s8-20260903/death-certificate.json, SHA-256 800ee629a708fa561610d2b0d014f6523b5b0d7bb0b80270720a2bac6064efd9, mechanically checks the residue row, the inverse 1/64, every Q-star pivot coefficient, exclusion of c, the embedded Singular fields, and the independent replay.
+
+## 5. The other declared branch
+
+The current frozen delta=2 stage-4 JSON has the charged SHA-256 5e9dd9516335ef5afa0bd956d014cf8050601ea960e284b6e5b0a6effef51. It records 118 constant residues after 35 cumulative Q-star pivots. The first one supplies the sufficient certificate
