+## 6. Stop rule and recomposition gate
+
+The branch died at the first newly requested band, so stage 9 was neither started nor emitted as a next-system manifest. Although the stage-8 JSON contains the engine's generic prospective next_stage description, the manifest helper has no license to serialize it after a DEAD result. There was no second unchanged dimension, no nonlinear surviving scheme, and no budget stop.
+
+The exact dimension never reached a nonempty value at or below 20. It moved from the accepted stage-7 value 869 to a stage-8 formal pre-residue generator count 862 and then to the unit ideal. Accordingly the exact-solve and recomposition gate was not activated. There is no point at which to reconstruct F,G; no direct polynomial identity check is possible or needed for a death certificate. In particular, this lane does not claim a genuine pair or a counterexample to JC2.
+
+## 7. Typed verdict and dependency gates
+
+The imposed finite subsystem consists of the charged common-h3/major-h2 state, outer base-h2 D2 support, the exhausted outer D1 rows, direct minor F,G rows, and direct Jacobian rows in the declared local branch. The charged sources license emptiness of this necessary subsystem as death of the branch inside chart (2.1); a nonempty quotient would have been only a counting bound. Therefore the exact typed conclusions are:
+
+    delta=5/2: DEAD[DECLARED-NECESSARY-FINITE-CHART].
+    both branches: NO-SURVIVING-BRANCH[DECLARED-(99,66)-JOINT-CHART].
+    conditional skeleton verdict: NO-KELLER-PAIR-WITH-THE-(99,66)-SKELETON.
+
+The last line depends jointly on all of the following gates:
+
+1. The displayed common-h3/major-h2 chart is necessary for every Keller pair with the (99,66) skeleton under consideration.
+2. The branch split delta in {2,5/2} is exhaustive and the branch equations, nonvanishing conditions (rho!=0 or c!=0), pole substitutions, and vertex/source hypotheses are correct.
+3. The outer D2/D1 support conditions, direct minor rows, and Jacobian rows used here are necessary, with strict-below support deletion kept distinct from at-level D1 parting and denominator shedding.
+4. The imported low-q K2c coordinate change is genuinely invertible and unit-triangular on the declared structural state, despite the full inverse to original C2,C3 names not being serialized.
+5. The pinned exact implementation represents those equations faithfully, and the two constant-unit/Singular certificates are accepted.
+
+The effective T2,T3 pi-root bridge remains typed OPEN[EFFECTIVE-T2-T3-BRIDGE] and was not imposed. Its omission weakens this necessary subsystem, so it cannot rescue a unit ideal. No unrestricted Jacobian-conjecture or other-skeleton verdict follows.
+
+The relevant charged scope statements are in g9966-global-band-sol56-20260903.md:9-30,163-176,258-347,396-419 and g9966-outer-bridge-grok46-20260903.md:234-245,332-339.
+
+## 8. FALLACY-v2 audit
+
